# Agent Safety Boundaries

> Agent 安全边界：禁止未审查提交、依赖验证、防御性操作

## Critical Boundaries (NEVER violate)

- NEVER commit code without user review
- NEVER delete config files (.env, package.json, mcp.json) without explicit confirmation
- NEVER run destructive git commands (push --force, hard reset) without explicit request
- NEVER modify authentication/authorization logic without presenting the plan first
- If you find a security vulnerability, STOP and report it immediately

## Defensive Operations

- Before multi-file refactoring: create a git checkpoint
- After every successful test run: commit immediately
- Never modify more than 5 files without an intermediate verification step
- 长时间运行的 agent session 中，每完成一个子任务就保存进度

## Dependency Verification

- Before importing an npm package: verify it exists in package.json or run `npm list <package>`
- Before importing a Python package: verify with `pip show <package>`
- NEVER assume a package exists based on training data — always verify at runtime
- When using framework APIs: verify the API exists in the current version

## Error Handling

- When an approach fails twice, step back and try a fundamentally different strategy
- If stuck in a loop, report the situation clearly rather than repeating the same action
- 遇到权限错误或网络错误时，报告问题而非无限重试